# Apply order and USE-flag grouping, mirroring src_prepare() in the overlay's
# single app-editors/zed ebuild -- resolved, never named. An overlay autoupdate
# bumps that ebuild most days, so a version written here is stale before anyone
# reads it; this header said zed-1.19.0_pre20260826-r1 while the tree packaged
# 1.19.0_pre20260829, three bumps later. `resolve_version` in scripts/lib.sh is
# how the tooling finds it.

# @feature: claude-agent-acp-plus
0001-force-enable-claude-agent-acp-plus.patch
# 0003/0004 (per-option _meta description + preview) retired: upstream 950ec79
# surfaces option descriptions natively via the ACP EnumOption.description
# field, superseding the _claude/askUserQuestionOption _meta machinery (and
# renamed MultiSelectItems::Untitled -> String). The numbers stay retired so
# the remaining filenames keep matching the ebuild's PATCHES+=() lines.
0005-elicitation-multiline-fields.patch
0006-elicitation-option-previews.patch
0007-manual-mode-badge.patch
0008-clickable-attachments.patch
# 0009: adopt the agent's config-option response when applying per-agent
# defaults, so options that appear as a side effect (Fast mode once the
# resolved model supports it) surface without a manual model switch.
0009-Adopt-agent-s-config-option-response-when-applying-d.patch
# 0010: a thread menu choice (permission mode, model, thinking effort, an ACP
# agent's config options) applies to that thread only; Shift also makes it the
# default for new threads. It applies to the packaged source on its own, so it
# rides this flag by choice rather than by dependency -- it also covers the
# native agent's own menus, which this flag otherwise has nothing to do with.
0010-shift-to-set-as-default.patch
# 0011: an "Account" section in the context tooltip, showing the account quota
# windows (5-hour, weekly, per-model) the adapter already forwards under
# _meta["_claude/rateLimit"] and Zed previously discarded. It rides this flag by
# dependency, not by choice: no other agent sends that key, so without the
# adapter the section never renders.
0011-account-usage-panel.patch
# 0012: a "Worktrees" entry in the agent panel's menu, dispatching the existing
# zero-argument zed_actions::git::Worktree so the picker decides between creating
# a worktree and switching to one. Zed already ships the capability end to end and
# the panel already reaches it -- but only under request.use_new_worktree, which is
# an input of the create_thread AGENT TOOL, so the model could open a worktree and
# the person looking at the same panel could not. It applies to the packaged source
# on its own, so like 0010 it rides this flag by choice rather than by dependency:
# nothing about a worktree needs the adapter.
0012-agent-panel-worktree-entry.patch
# 0013: the model-scoped quota window. The adapter forwards every
# rate_limits.model_scoped[] entry under the single wire kind "model_scoped",
# and from_wire had no arm for it, so the per-model row 0011's Account section
# was built to show never arrived. Adds a dynamic variant carrying the
# server-supplied display name -- it adds a name, it does not open the enum:
# an unrecognised kind is still dropped. Rides this flag BY DEPENDENCY, like
# 0011: no other agent sends that key.
0013-model-scoped-quota-window.patch
# 0014: a copy button on the user's own message, returning the string the edit
# path already serialises (ContentBlock::to_markdown, what the LostFocus handler
# compares against) rather than a second serialisation. The button sits on the
# shared container before the editable/non-editable branch, so subagent messages
# -- always non-editable -- get it too. Pure Zed affordance, so it rides this
# flag BY CHOICE, the way 0010 and 0012 do.
0014-copy-the-user-s-own-message.patch
# 0015: the thread archive scoped to its project. Three reads were global, not
# one: the list, the ArchivedOnly fall-back guard, and the archived-only
# toggle's own disabled state. Deliberately NOT via the store's entries_for_path
# -- that reader drops archived threads, which is correct for the sidebar and
# fatal for an archive view. Pure Zed, BY CHOICE.
0015-scoped-thread-history.patch
# 0016: a rendered-markdown preview of the composer's draft, through the same
# MarkdownElement that draws every agent response. Reached by the
# ToggleMessagePreview action (command palette; bindable). The source is
# re-derived on each toggle and refreshed on edit -- an Entity<Markdown> built
# once renders the first draft forever while passing every two-step test. Pure
# Zed, BY CHOICE, and the only one of the five that is new UI rather than an
# affordance over existing machinery.
0016-composer-markdown-preview.patch
# 0017: native rendering for a compaction the adapter reports. The ACP
# compaction_update variant is unreachable here -- agent-client-protocol 2.0.0
# and -schema 1.5.0 contain zero occurrences of "compaction" -- so this reads
# the adapter's versioned _meta.contextCompaction and dispatches into the
# EXISTING push_context_compaction. An unknown version falls through to the
# generic tool row untouched. Both the opening and terminal frames are consumed
# at the same seam, or update_tool_call fabricates a "Tool call not found"
# failure row beside the entry. Rides this flag BY DEPENDENCY: only this adapter
# emits that key.
0017-native-compaction-entry.patch

